# App layout

This repo is one tree. `main.ts` is the `serve()` callback and boots it.

A **page** is a folder that exports handlers (`Home`, `list`, `add`). Nested,
page-local components live in that folder. `main.ts` binds
`route("/path", { GET: Home })`. One module = one path. One-offs such as
`staticFile` stay on `main.ts`.

`group()` is only for a prefixed subtree (nested paths, or layouts /
middleware / `notFound` on that prefix) or a pathless wrap shell. A one-path
page, including `/` and `/docs`, is handlers bound on the root table.

## File names

Deno snake_case. Feature folders match the path (`docs/` for `/docs`).
Layout and middleware files are `{folder}_{role}`: `menu_layout.tsx`,
`menu_middleware.ts`. Nested `reviews/` uses `reviews_layout.tsx`. At the app
root: `root_layout.tsx`, `logger_middleware.ts`, `errors.tsx`. Client modules
are `*_client.ts` (`clock_client.ts`) and sit beside the file that registers
them. No `routes/` directory, no app `client/` folder, no `_` magic prefixes,
and no `*_route.tsx`.

`errors.tsx` holds the named `notFound`, `error`, and `fatal`
exports. Those are not routes. Root `notFound` / `error` live on the root
callback; a group's `notFound` / `error` live on that group's `mod.ts`.
`fatal` stays on `serve()` options.

Ordinary extra modules (`todos.ts`, later `db.ts`) sit beside the handlers.
No blessed view / service / DAL layer: extract `menu_service.ts` or a
component when needed. No `layouts/` or `middleware/` folders.

## Exports

A component that returns `Element` is PascalCase (`Home`, `RootLayout`,
`ErrorPage`). Middleware and per-method handlers are camelCase (`logger`,
`list`, `add`). Do not export `GET` as the function name. Do not export a
`{ GET: Home }` bag.

`mod.ts` (`mod.tsx` when the file contains JSX) is the page module: handlers
in that file. No `*_route.tsx` and no `controller.ts` inside a page folder.
Only the root table in `main.ts` names the path and the methods.

## Table

`main.ts` is the `serve()` callback. It binds `route()` for every page and
any root one-offs, then calls `serve`. Page folders export handlers. The
root table is the only place that calls `route()`. Do not `import { group }`
inside a bag callback. Do not export `route()`.

```tsx
// home/mod.tsx
export function Home() {
  return <h1>dashi.run</h1>;
}
```

`group("/", …)` is illegal. Pathless `group(({ route }) => …)` is a
layout/middleware shell with no extra prefix. A pre-built `Group` types
`ctx.params` from its own prefix; nested groups do not read ancestor params
they did not declare. Shared data goes on `ctx.state`.

`main.ts` is:

```ts
import { CacheStrategy, serve, staticFile } from "dashi";
import { Home } from "./home/mod.tsx";
import { RootLayout } from "./root_layout.tsx";
import { error, fatal, notFound } from "./errors.tsx";

if (import.meta.main) {
  serve(({ route }) => ({
    layouts: [RootLayout],
    notFound,
    error,
    routes: [
      route("/", { GET: Home }),
      route("/static/:file", {
        GET: (ctx) =>
          staticFile(ctx, `${import.meta.dirname}/static`, ctx.params.file, {
            strategy: CacheStrategy.Immutable,
          }),
      }),
      route("/generated/:file", {
        GET: (ctx) =>
          staticFile(ctx, `${import.meta.dirname}/generated`, ctx.params.file, {
            strategy: CacheStrategy.Immutable,
          }),
      }),
    ],
  }), { fatal });
}
```

Later pages are the same: `docs/mod.tsx` exports `Docs`; `main.ts` binds
`route("/docs", { GET: Docs })`.

A prefixed group is a URL subtree. The parent drops that `Group` into
`routes`:

```ts
import { group } from "dashi";

export const account = group("/account", ({ route }) => ({
  layouts: [AccountLayout],
  routes: [
    route("/", { GET: AccountHome }),
    route("/settings", { GET: Settings }),
  ],
}));
```

## Imports

App code imports from `dashi`. JSX types (`Element`, `HTMLAttributes`,
`DashiNode`, `JSX`) import from `dashi/jsx-runtime`. Browser APIs import
from `dashi/client`.
